<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Worktree GC (BRO-2608). Runs scripts/gc-merged-worktrees.sh hourly —
         the only automated brake on disk growth from abandoned worktrees.
         data/audit/worktree-gc.log's freshness is watched by
         scripts/lib/worktree-gc-freshness.js (health-check.js's "Infra:
         worktree GC log stale" row); a silent stop here previously ran 5
         days before anyone noticed, disk falling from 88Gi to 26Gi free.

         Was untracked (only ever lived in ~/Library/LaunchAgents) until
         BRO-3635: the plist was not recoverable from the repo, and the
         health-check hint told an operator to "check launchctl print" and
         "run the script manually" — neither of which fixes a launchd job
         that has stopped firing (BRO-3635: `launchctl print` showed the job
         loaded with `last exit code = 0`, the Mac had not slept or rebooted
         in 24 days, yet NEITHER trigger had fired in ~4 days — not just the
         hourly StartInterval but also the independent 04:00
         StartCalendarInterval backstop, confirmed absent from the log across
         three consecutive 04:00 windows. Both triggers going dark points at
         the whole job/session having gone stale in launchd's bookkeeping,
         not a StartInterval-specific bug — `launchctl print` does not surface
         this, and running the script by hand only refreshes the log without
         restoring either schedule). A bootout+bootstrap reload immediately
         let a forced `kickstart` produce a real run again; that proves the
         reload unwedged it, but only an UNFORCED run on the next natural
         trigger (top of the hour, or the next 04:00) proves the schedule
         itself is restored — check data/audit/worktree-gc.log for one before
         considering a recurrence closed. The fix is tracked here so it
         survives a lost plist and is one copy-paste away next time.

         StartInterval (3600s) is the primary cadence; StartCalendarInterval
         04:00 local is a daily backstop — though BRO-3635 shows a wedge can
         take out both at once, so the backstop is not a substitute for
         verifying the freshness check itself stays green. An array of dicts
         is unneeded here since there's only one entry, but see
         claude-auth-health.plist for that pattern.

         Install:  cp scripts/launchd/com.broadwayscore.worktree-gc.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
                   launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.worktree-gc 2>/dev/null
                   launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.broadwayscore.worktree-gc.plist
         Manual run: launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.worktree-gc
         Kill:     launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.worktree-gc
         If the "Infra: worktree GC log stale" health-check row fires again
         and the job is loaded but simply not firing (the BRO-3635 case —
         not a disabled/missing job), the fix is the reload above, not just
         a manual script run. -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.broadwayscore.worktree-gc</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/tompryor/Broadwayscore/scripts/gc-merged-worktrees.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/tompryor/Broadwayscore</string>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>3600</integer>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>4</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/tompryor/Broadwayscore/data/audit/worktree-gc.launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/tompryor/Broadwayscore/data/audit/worktree-gc.launchd.log</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
